{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1172027-infernal-investments-and-you","id":1172027,"title":"Infernal Investments and You!","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Mage: The Ascension"],"posts":[{"date":"2017-12-31T10:47:11-08:00","id":1172027,"title":"Infernal Investments and You!","content":"So, a player in an upcoming game is wanting to play an infernalist on the run from their fate and trying to redeem themself. I trust the player to roleplay this well. <br /> <br /> The issue I have before me is that the player wants some infernal investments and I need to figure out how to cost them. I immediately decided that using Soul Points is not a fair option as the character's goal is to save their soul (essentially) and extra powers should come with extra cost. So, I narrowed it down to a couple of potential options and I would like some input from people with insight into this.<br /> <br /> 1) Say no. Because this is a very valid response.<br /> 2) Make each Investment cost an amount of freebies based on its cost.<br /> 3) Make Investments into a Background with each dot granting so many points.<br /> 4) Make it a Merit to have investment points (like Laham from Path of Screams, but modified)<br /> 5) Someone on the forums has a much better idea.<br /> <br /> With any option besides 1 I intend to roll for their Soul, as in Book of madness, secretly and use that as a guide for a guide with the plot to save themself (if they can)...<br /> <br /> If anyone has any suggestions, thoughts, or mechanically expertise I would be very grateful for the help.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8764-zulkir-jhor","name":"Zulkir Jhor","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8764_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"26"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-31T12:14:32-08:00","id":1172044,"title":"","content":"Modify Rotes to make for Investments, and then let the PC change from the &quot;Investment&quot; to the normal Rote as redemption takes away the pact.<br /> <br /> Take examples from the Demon Lores in DtF, on how they change from Low-Torment to High-Torment. An Investment would be a &quot;High-Torment&quot; version of a Rote, buffed but out of control.<br /> <br /> Investments based on Spheres the character doesn't have could cost a fourth of the XP to buy the missing dots, but as part of redemption the character needs to complete the cost and buy the full dots, learning that aspect of the Tellurian only previously known through the pact.<br /> <br /> Also, though the Investments can seem to be free of Paradox, they could bring Paradox-like effects based on corruption and torment.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":5826,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","user":"monteparnas","date":". 12-31-2017, 03:26 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-31T14:04:09-08:00","id":1172067,"title":"","content":"Making the Investments cost Freebie points would probably be the simplest way of running it. If so, you might consider mandating that the runaway Infernalist take some hefty Flaws to pay for them. You know, to represent the downsides to having made the deal, and to represent skipping out on the patron and trying to go straight. Flaws like Haunted (for a spiritual agent of the patron), Blood Magick (if the character learned their magick through the Investment), Primal Marks, Uncanny, Gremlin (a Familiar given by the patron, who is now angry at the character's betrayal), Immortal Enemy (the patron themselves), Jinx (an infernal Wonder that the character just can't get rid of), or even Taint of Corruption (which likely fits the idea the player is going for best).<br /> <br /> All of these can be found in the Book of Secrets, and some of them can be found in the older books.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://archiveofourown.org/works/6956863/chapters/15862327\" target=\"_blank\">Magestuck: The Ascension</a></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6156-bluecho","name":"Bluecho","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6156_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3871"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-31T14:25:26-08:00","id":1172070,"title":"","content":"It's also worth remembering that while demons want souls most of all, they aren't above making deals for other things. Things like favors, information, prized possessions, first born children, etc. The character might have traded something other than their soul, and now feels bad about it.<br /> <br /> Another Flaw the character could take is Branded, signifying that the character made an infernal deal and got caught. Which sect they belong to could have branded their aura as punishment, in order to display to everyone (with supernatural senses, that is) that the character danced with the devil. In practice, of course, groups like the Traditions would only use a Brand for a lesser form of Infernalism, like as described above. Outright selling one's soul - in whole or in part - usually results in a harsher punishment (like Death or even Gilgul), unless their punishment was lessened for some reason (some higher up mage pulled some strings, for instance).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://archiveofourown.org/works/6956863/chapters/15862327\" target=\"_blank\">Magestuck: The Ascension</a></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6156-bluecho","name":"Bluecho","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6156_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3871"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-31T21:29:44-08:00","id":1172168,"title":"","content":"Thanks for the input. I think this all gives me a good place to start from.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8764-zulkir-jhor","name":"Zulkir Jhor","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8764_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"26"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-01T03:59:16-08:00","id":1172225,"title":"","content":"I would say this would be justification for merits and the background blessing?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2715-lian","name":"Lian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-05T18:33:22-08:00","id":1173657,"title":"","content":"I would go for the background thing but make the infernalism constantly bite him in the ass. He wanted the power, well, he got it. Now he has to deal with the consequences. If it just translates to normal char creation it was even less worth it. Unless you want to go with the party being particularly special and his char only being so _because_ of the infernal pact. That might be an alternative.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4017-angryicecream","name":"angryicecream","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"191"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-08T12:00:41-08:00","id":1174326,"title":"","content":"I once played a mage character with exactly this premise. Investments (and a dot in Linguistics to understand the Dragon's Tongue) were bought with freebie points paid for via the Dark Secret, Nightmares, and Demon-Plagued Flaws.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3505-matt-the-bruins-fan","name":"Matt the Bruins fan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3505_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2401"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-16T16:52:29-08:00","id":1186869,"title":"","content":"I would consider backgrounds, like enhancements.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Be correct.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23728-pewpew","name":"PewPew","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"107"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-17T04:25:08-08:00","id":1187004,"title":"","content":"I'd take a devil may care additude to the whole thing. Be impish and make them a deal. Remember lots of fine print.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/857-astromancer","name":"Astromancer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar857_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2195"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-19T15:12:50-08:00","id":1187662,"title":"","content":"Iirc, VtM has rules for infernal investments in their older supplements (2nd edition and VtDA). Will come back later if i manage to dig up more info","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://imageshack.com/i/j5vvlqp\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/i/j5vvlqp\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/ghw20supporterhiddengaroup\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/n18segp\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/0v25ewp\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><br /> <br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#404040\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\">English is not my native language, so i apologize for errors in grammar or spelling.</span></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/392-cadmiumcadamium","name":"Cadmiumcadamium","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar392_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"936"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-19T15:49:16-08:00","id":1187669,"title":"","content":"Alternative idea: Let the player have whatever infernal gifts they want, free of charge.<br /> <br /> Now, keep track of any time the player uses or benefits from these infernal gifts, and think about what his demon buddies might wish to do. Have them turn up and remind him of their deal, and that their gifts can be easily taken away, or even reversed if they don't follow through.<br /> <br /> Are they able to heal instantly from any disease? Great, just after a huge battle, while all the other players are patching up their wounds, have the demon beckon our infernalist over and remind him of their part in his success. That the demon basically saved their life. Start with guilt, and see if they agree to do something small for the demon, something which doesn't seem so bad like making a delivery, or making sure a certain doctor doesn't catch the morning train. If guilt works, then be sure to ramp it up slowly, perhaps even offer a few more rewards. If guilt doesn't work, consider moving on to abuse, make the infernalist consider they are nothing without the demon's support.<br /> Other tactics can involve messing with the guys head. &quot;You want out? All you had to do was say so&quot;, contract revoked, powers lost, and then the mage is thrust into situations in which those powers would have been the exact thing they needed to get out of them. Demon appears asking if they changed their mind, though now the price will be much steeper than before.<br /> Does the player flat out defy the demon? Great, turn every benefit they received into a curse. Able to fly? good like being able to stay on the ground. Everlasting youth? Prepare to age in reverse to the point of becoming a baby. Or even reverse the effects, super healing powers gone and all the damage they didn't receive hits them like a hurricane.<br /> <br /> Just because the player bought it at character creation does not make them sacred, especially if they came from infernal origins.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/959615-chronicle-report-keepers-of-the-wyck\" target=\"_blank\">Keepers of the Wyck: A Chronicle I'm running</a> FINALE: Chapter 39: Green Fairy","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12193-saikou","name":"Saikou","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12193_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1406"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}